---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Tag from "../../components/docs/Tag.astro";

const config = `# ~/.coding.sh/config.toml  (coding.sh config get prints the effective values)
[store]
index = "sqlite://~/.coding.sh/index.db"
blobs = "file://~/.coding.sh/blobs"

[capture]
mode = "full"                 # or "metadata": no prompts, code or tool output
redact = ["secrets"]          # "secrets", "env", or "none"
redactPatterns = []           # extra regexes
exclude = []                  # repo globs never captured
maxInlineBytes = 4096         # larger payloads move to blobs

[retention]
keepSpoolDays = 7
toolOutputDays = 90`;

const purge = `coding.sh purge --literal leaked.txt --dry-run   # count the copies
coding.sh purge --literal leaked.txt             # replace them
coding.sh purge --rule 'sk-ant-api03-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{80,}'   # every match of a shape`;

const sinks = `[[sinks]]
kind = "otlp"                           # OTLP/HTTP JSON traces to {endpoint}/v1/traces
name = "collector"
endpoint = "http://localhost:4318"
mode = "metadata"                       # the default for every sink

[[sinks]]
kind = "http"                           # POSTs {schema, v, mode, events, sessions}
endpoint = "https://relay.example.com/ingest"
mode = "full"
headers = { Authorization = "Bearer \${RELAY_TOKEN}" }   # read from the environment`;

const plugin = `// coding.sh-store-postgres/index.mjs (the real package, abridged)
export function indexStore(url, config) {
  return PgIndexStore.open(url);   // resolves to an IndexStore
}

// coding.sh-sink-kafka/index.mjs (hypothetical package)
export function sink(sinkConfig, config) {
  return { name: sinkConfig.name ?? "kafka", mode: sinkConfig.mode, async write(events, sessions, blobs) { /* … */ return { ok: true }; } };
}`;

const iface = `interface IndexStore {
  readonly kind: string;
  migrate(): Promise<void>;
  close(): Promise<void>;
  putEvents(batch: AgentEvent[]): Promise<{ inserted: number }>;   // idempotent on event.id
  upsertSession(session: Session): Promise<void>;
  getSession(id: string): Promise<Session | undefined>;
  listSessions(filter?: SessionFilter): Promise<Session[]>;
  listEvents(sessionId: string, opts?: { kinds?: string[]; limit?: number; offset?: number }): Promise<AgentEvent[]>;
  search(text: string, opts?: { limit?: number; agent?: string }): Promise<SearchHit[]>;
  getCursor(source: string): Promise<number>;
  setCursor(source: string, offset: number): Promise<void>;
  // plus tasks, harness bundles, runs, labels, referencedBlobs(),
  // and optional datasets, experiments, judges, kv state and compact()
}

interface BlobStore {
  readonly kind: string;
  put(data: Uint8Array | string): Promise<string>;   // returns the sha256; dedupes
  get(ref: string): Promise<Uint8Array | undefined>;
  getText(ref: string): Promise<string | undefined>;
  has(refs: string[]): Promise<boolean[]>;
  list(): AsyncIterable<string>;
  delete(ref: string): Promise<void>;
}

interface Sink {
  readonly name: string;
  readonly mode: "full" | "metadata";
  write(batch: AgentEvent[], sessions: Session[], blobs: BlobStore): Promise<{ ok: boolean; error?: string; retryAfterMs?: number }>;
}`;
---

<DocsLayout>
  <p>
    coding.sh keeps two stores with different shapes, plus any number of write-only mirrors. All three are interfaces
    (<code>src/core/types.ts</code>), chosen by URL scheme in the config.
  </p>

  <h2 id="index">Index <Tag status="built" /></h2>
  <p>
    Small, queryable rows: sessions, events, eval tasks, harness bundles, runs, labels, datasets and experiments. The default is one SQLite file
    through the built-in <code>node:sqlite</code>, in WAL mode, with an FTS5 table over prompt, reply and tool text for
    <code>coding.sh search</code>. Writes are idempotent on event id, so re-ingesting the same spool changes nothing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/cli/sql"><code>coding.sh sql "select …"</code></a> runs one read-only query against it.
    <a href="/docs/cli/export"><code>coding.sh export sessions|events|labels</code></a> streams rows as JSONL or CSV, on every store. The tables
    and columns are in <a href="https://github.com/jackulau/coding.sh/blob/main/docs/reference/query.md">Query and export</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="blobs">Blobs <Tag status="built" /></h2>
  <p>
    Large, write-once content: full tool output, raw source payloads, diffs. Event payloads larger than <code>maxInlineBytes</code> (4 KB)
    move to a blob and the event keeps a reference. Each blob is keyed by the sha256 of its uncompressed bytes, so the same
    <code>AGENTS.md</code> read in a thousand sessions is stored once.
  </p>
  <p>
    Blobs are compressed with zstd level 3. One that compresses to under 4 KiB is a row of <code>blobs/pack.db</code> (SQLite); a larger one
    is <code>blobs/ab/cd/&lt;sha256&gt;.zst</code>, written to a temp file then renamed, so readers never see half a blob.
  </p>

  <h2 id="config">Config</h2>
  <Code title="config.toml" code={config} />
  <p>
    A repository can carry its own <code>.coding.sh/config.toml</code>, but because it arrives with <code>git clone</code> it is untrusted: it
    may only tighten capture (add redaction, exclusions or metadata mode) and adjust snapshot settings. It can never add a sink or move a store, which would let a repository send your
    sessions somewhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Redaction and metadata mode</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Redaction runs before anything is written to the index, blobs or sinks. The built-in <code>secrets</code> rules key on vendor token prefixes and on secret-looking names next to values, so code, paths and hashes pass through.</li>
    <li><code>capture.mode = "metadata"</code> keeps ids, timings, kinds, counts and usage, and drops prompts, code and tool output.</li>
    <li>A session in which a vendor token was redacted gets the <code>secret:exposed</code> tag: the agent and its model provider saw it, so rotate it. <code>coding.sh sessions --flag secret:exposed</code> lists them.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/how-to/capture-with-proxy">The model API proxy</a> redacts each request and response before storing it, and never stores <code>Authorization</code>, <code>x-api-key</code> or cookies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A value that got past redaction can be removed afterwards. Put it in a file, one value per line, and count the copies first:</p>
  <Code code={purge} />
  <p>
    Every copy is replaced, in the index, blobs, spool and eval runs: with <code>[redacted:purged]</code> in the index and blobs, with asterisks in spool and eval run files. SQLite store only; rotate the secret too.
    <a href="/docs/cli/purge">purge</a> has the details, and
    <a href="https://github.com/jackulau/coding.sh/blob/main/docs/guides/privacy.md">Storage, sinks and privacy</a> covers every redaction rule.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sinks">Sinks <Tag status="built" /></h2>
  <p>
    A sink mirrors events to somewhere else. Each sink keeps its own cursor and retries with backoff, so a remote that is down never blocks
    local capture. Remote sinks default to <code>metadata</code> mode: content leaves your machine only when you set <code>mode = "full"</code>.
  </p>
  <Code title="config.toml" code={sinks} />
  <ul>
    <li><strong><code>otlp</code></strong>: OTLP/HTTP JSON. A session becomes an <code>invoke_agent</code> span, tools <code>execute_tool</code> spans and replies <code>chat</code> spans, with <code>gen_ai.*</code> attributes pinned to semconv 1.37.0. Span ids derive from event ids, so a resent batch de-duplicates.</li>
    <li><strong><code>http</code></strong>: posts coding.sh/trace JSON as is, for a collector or relay that speaks it.</li>
    <li>Sinks mirror hook events at ingest, and events from the <a href="/docs/otel">OTLP receiver</a>. <code>coding.sh serve</code> mirrors every batch it commits to the sinks in its own config, so a team can set one there instead of on each laptop.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="remote">Plugging in a remote store</h2>
  <p>
    Built-in schemes are <code>sqlite://</code> and <code>memory://</code> for the index, and <code>file://</code> and
    <code>memory://</code> for blobs. For any other scheme the CLI imports an npm package by convention:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>coding.sh-store-&lt;scheme&gt;</code> exporting <code>indexStore(url, config)</code> and/or <code>blobStore(url, config)</code>;</li>
    <li><code>coding.sh-sink-&lt;kind&gt;</code> exporting <code>sink(sinkConfig, config)</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The package must be resolvable from where coding.sh is installed. A missing package gives an error that names it; a package that fails to
    load surfaces its own error.
  </p>
  <Code title="javascript" code={plugin} />
  <p>
    The interfaces a plugin implements, abridged. A test suite in <code>src/store/conformance.ts</code> runs against the built-in stores and
    can be pointed at a new one.
  </p>
  <Code title="src/core/types.ts (abridged)" code={iface} />
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Postgres, ClickHouse and S3:</strong> <code>coding.sh-store-postgres</code>, <code>coding.sh-store-clickhouse</code> and
      <code>coding.sh-store-s3</code> (S3, R2, MinIO) are on npm and back <a href="/docs/production">production mode</a>. Install one next to
      coding.sh. The npm package ships the TypeScript types for <code>coding.sh/store</code> and <code>coding.sh/store/conformance</code>, so a
      plugin built outside the repository imports them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gc">Retention and gc</h2>
  <p>
    <code>coding.sh gc</code> deletes spool files older than <code>keepSpoolDays</code> once every sink has them, tool-output blobs older than
    <code>toolOutputDays</code> (diffs and eval tasks are kept), and unreferenced blobs, and trims the judge cache to its size cap. <code>--compact</code> also runs
    SQLite <code>VACUUM</code>; <code>--dry-run</code> shows what would go.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
